Package: NeuralForest
Title: Adaptive Neural-Guided Random Forests
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Quentin", "Lamboley", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "145555916+QuentinLamboley@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: A native C++17 random forest engine for classification and regression
    augmented by an out-of-bag neural difficulty learner. A neural network learns
    observation priorities and guides subsequent bootstrap samples and feature
    selection. Includes distribution-aware presets, metric-driven selection,
    cross-validation, and transparent diagnostic and benchmarking functions.
    This is an experimental research implementation, not an established
    replacement for 'ranger'.
License: CC0
URL: https://github.com/QuentinLamboley/NeuralForest
BugReports: https://github.com/QuentinLamboley/NeuralForest/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.3.0)
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.12), stats, utils
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), ranger
SystemRequirements: C++17 compiler
NeedsCompilation: yes
Config/testthat/edition: 3
